      "id": "MACUI-01",
      "severity": "P2",
      "title": "Quit guidance promises cancellation until after the actual cutoff",
      "location": {
        "path": "apps/macos-launcher/Presentation/PresentationCopy.swift",
        "line": 121,
        "endLine": 121
      },
      "trigger": "With progress visible, let the worker win AttemptState.commit. Deliver Quit before the worker invokes the native gateway spawn.",
      "impact": "The progress window promises cancellation while GraphGoblin has yet to start. Startup can still proceed after Quit because the commit has already won. This includes the Starting stage, which the worker emits after commitment and before spawn.",
      "correction": "Make the progress text reflect that Quit cancels a pending start and that an already committed start may still finish. Preserve the existing Hide and detached-gateway semantics. Update the fixed-copy expectation.",
